<h1>Erin Ross</h1>
<p>19th Ward alderman, on the Chicago ballot February 23, 2027.</p>
<p><a href="https://www.erinross19.com/" rel="nofollow noopener">Campaign site (erinross19.com)</a></p>
<h2>Running on</h2>
<p>Running for the open seat with the endorsement of retiring Ald. Matt O&#39;Shea, who announced in September 2026 that he will not seek a fifth term. She says she wants to work more closely with community groups, create more opportunities for community engagement and gatherings, and support first responders at a time of reduced police staffing. Her campaign site&#39;s slogan is &quot;Safe streets. Strong schools. Thriving businesses.&quot; and it does not yet publish a detailed platform.</p>
<h2>Background</h2>
<p>Chief of staff in the 19th Ward office since 2024; previously executive director of the 95th Street Business Association for more than a decade. Lifelong Beverly resident.</p>
